   "widgets_values": [
    "## sprite-atlas.json\n\nCombine individual sprites into one sheet\n\n**Does:** packs four separate images into one 2x2 sheet with core `ImageGridComposite2x2` - swap the `LoadImage` nodes for your own files. It ships the four 64 px potion sprites, so it runs as-is and reproduces `input/2d/potion_atlas.png` exactly (verified pixel-identical).\n**Other counts:** `ImageBatchMulti` (`inputcount`, then `image_1`...) feeds a generic `ImageGrid` (`columns`, `cell_width`, `cell_height`, `padding`) - use that pair for anything that is not 2x2 or 3x3. Those extra inputs are created by the frontend, so a headless replica must build them by hand.\n**No generation here:** make the sprites with `pixel-art.json` (or convert an existing picture with `pixel-art-convert.json` / `pixel-art-restyle.json`), then pack them.\n**Unpacking?** `sprite-slice.json` turns a sheet back into tiles and proves the round-trip in the same run.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E6/E33** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
